               <p xml:id="idm162">1884-1889 the Schimmelmann Mansion in Bredgade in Copenhagen (the present Odd Fellow Mansion) was extended with a concert hall in the former garden. In 1888, before it was finished, it was used for the Nordic Music Festival. After the inauguration all the concerts of Musikforeningen took place in "Koncertpalæet" as it was then called. The hall was considered the best in Copenhagen with fine acoustics, until it burned down in 1992. It was not rebuilt.</p>
            </history>
